# Laravel API JSON responses

All API responses must be JSON with this structure:

- **`message`**: string (success or error message; may be `null` on error) — **required**
- **`data`**: mixed|null (payload; `null` on error) — **required**
- **`error`**: string|null (error message when applicable; `null` on success) — **optional**
- **`status`**: integer (HTTP-style code: 200, 201, 400, 401, 404, etc.) — **optional**

Use the standardized response helper on the base Controller class (or equivalent project helper).

Examples:

- Success: `{ "message": "Operation successful", "data": {...} }`
- Success (all fields): `{ "message": "Operation successful", "error": null, "data": {...}, "status": 200 }`
- Error: `{ "message": "Error description", "data": null }`
- Error (all fields): `{ "message": null, "error": "Error description", "data": null, "status": 400 }`
